      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Single-phase ZrB2 typically requires sintering above 2300 °C to achieve full density.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower-temperature processing leaves ZrB2 with inadequate oxidation and corrosion resistance.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding a few weight percent Si to ZrB2 powder can act as a sintering aid.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si addition enables ZrB2 densification at 1500–1700 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si produces a transient liquid phase during sintering.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed transient liquid phase improves densification and microstructural uniformity.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si promotes in-situ formation of an amorphous intergranular SiO2 layer during oxidizing or liquid-metal exposure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiO2 layer passivates ZrB2 grain boundaries.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiO2 layer limits oxygen diffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiO2 layer limits liquid-metal penetration.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si-doped ZrB2 will achieve near-full density after sintering at 1500–1700 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si-doped ZrB2 processed at 1500–1700 °C will have mechanical strength comparable to or greater than ZrB2 sintered above 2300 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si-doped ZrB2 will oxidize more slowly than pure ZrB2 and prior lower-temperature specimens.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si-doped ZrB2 will resist liquid plating-metal corrosion better than pure ZrB2 and prior lower-temperature specimens.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective silica layer can remain effective in oxidation service up to approximately 1600 °C.",
